From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe: Allow a pixel pipeline with its own output formats

The PIX line of a VFE either passes its input through like an RDI or,
on the gen1 VFEs, converts YUV 4:2:2 input. A Titan 17x IFE pixel
pipeline demosaics Bayer input into YUV 4:2:0, so its sink and source
pads carry different kinds of formats.

Add formats_pix_out to the VFE resources. If it is set for a full VFE,
the PIX line accepts formats_pix on its sink pad, offers
formats_pix_out on its source pad independently of the Bayer order of
the sink, and its video node uses formats_pix_out. The sink pad falls
back to its first supported code instead of UYVY, and compose and crop
keep the chroma sample alignment of 4:2:0.

Add the SC8280XP Bayer input and NV12/NV21 output tables. Nothing uses
them yet.

